And all the things I have shown you that by working hard in this way, we must help the weak and remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how he himself said, it is more blessed to receive.

225
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,800
He said all of these things.

226
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:26,280
He knelt down and prayed with them, and there was much weeping on the part of all of them.

227
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:33,560
They embraced Paul, and they kissed him, being sorrowful most of all because of the word that he had spoken, that they would not see his face again.

228
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:35,920
And they accompanied him to the ship.

229
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:36,900
You can sit down.

230
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:47,380
So, Paul had spent about two years of his life doing ministry in the city of Ephesus.

231
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:49,860
He had great affection for these people.

232
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:56,160
He calls their leadership to him, knowing that he will likely not ever be in Ephesus again or see their faces.

233
00:14:56,160 --> 00:15:07,260
He wants to give them a final reminder of how to lead the church, and he starts by giving them a testimony of how he started the church, of what he did in leading the church.

234
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:17,240
He gives a brief description of what his ministry was like in Ephesus, which I think is a good summary of what most of his ministry was like in a lot of the cities.

235
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:25,620
As you read the book of Exodus, you get this pattern that Saul or Paul led with throughout his visits to the cities.

236
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:26,400
This is what it looks like.

237
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:33,860
He would go to the synagogue, the Jewish temple, the Jewish gathering space on Sabbath, and he would begin to proclaim the message of the gospel.

238
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:54,040
What would happen in the synagogue is that some Jews and some what the Bible calls God-fearers, which is just Greeks who would go to church in the synagogue because they were interested in the things of Yahweh.

239
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:58,460
Some Jews, some God-fearers, would accept the gospel of Jesus with gladness.

240
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:00,660
Many Jews would get furious.

241
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:05,300
They would run Saul out of the synagogue or Paul, and they wouldn't want anything to do with him.

242
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:08,280
And so then he would turn to the Gentiles.

243
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:19,100
He would go to a secular meeting space, and he would proclaim the same message, that the resurrected Jesus is Israel's Messiah, that everything has changed, the way in which we live, our lives should change.

244
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:22,020
Some Gentiles would receive that message.

245
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:23,640
Others would get furious.

246
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:33,460
Then what would happen sometimes is the Jews and the Gentiles who were furious, they would kind of come together and run Saul out of town or try and kill him.

247
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:36,320
And this happened over and over and over again.

248
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:42,980
And Saul would work with the people who had received the message with gladness, and he would start a church.

249
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:51,100
He would raise up leaders, and he would encourage them to be faithful to the message of the gospel, to keep sharing that message, and he would go on to the next city.

250
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:52,040
Does that make sense?

251
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:55,540
Okay, so that had happened with Saul in Ephesus.

252
00:16:55,540 --> 00:17:04,600
He'd spent a long time there, and he is telling them, look, this is what happened to me in your city.

253
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,260
Look in verse 19.

254
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:13,280
He said, I served you with all humility and with tears and with trials that happened to me through the plots of the Jews.

255
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:18,540
He said, I did everything I could to preach the message faithfully, and yet I got persecuted.

256
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:22,140
He got persecuted by the Jews.

257
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:23,680
He got persecuted by the Gentiles.

258
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:27,180
Everywhere he went, he got persecuted.

259
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:32,660
Now, why is it that he got persecuted by both Jews and Gentiles?

260
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:48,180
Well, in verse 20, no, 21, he summarizes his message, and the message that he is sharing is the reason why he offends so many Jews and so many Gentiles all throughout his ministry.

261
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:53,400
Remember I said that this is like a snapshot of everything that he did in all of the cities?

262
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:57,380
This sentence right here in verse 21, this is a summary.

263
00:17:57,380 --> 00:18:07,120
Although Paul preached lots of other things, if you want to know the gist, the one sentence, thesis statement of Paul's message that he preached in all of his cities, that everywhere he went, this is what he preached.

264
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:29,340
This is the message that Paul preached that made many Jews and many Gentiles try and kill him over and over and over again from city to city to city.

265
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:37,640
To the Jews and to the Greeks, I proclaimed repentance towards God and faith in the Lord Jesus.

266
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,740
This is the message.

267
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:41,780
Does this sound familiar to any of us?

268
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:44,520
Does this sound like the gospel that we've heard preached from time to time?

269
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:47,720
There's some similarities there.

270
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:49,540
There's some familiarity there.

271
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:50,780
But here's what happens.

272
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:57,840
I think in the American church, this seemingly simple statement, we've become way too familiar with it.

273
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:01,960
It's just the thing that we've heard growing up over and over again.

274
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,840
It's the thing that we sing in our songs.

275
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:07,580
It's the phrase that we say and we repeat and we agree with.

276
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:10,500
And yet I think we lose sight of what it actually means.

277
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:13,600
We lose sight of the implications that it has on our lives.

278
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:21,500
And we lose sight of how in the world this simple, basic message could have flipped the entire world upside down in the first century.

279
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:35,360
Over and over again, from city to city to city, people heard this message and they were either offended and tried to persecute Paul and his crew or they submitted their entire lives to it.

280
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:40,700
This isn't some generic spiritual statement that we just sing in a song or tack on to the end of a prayer.

281
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:48,240
This message that Paul is preaching has incredible implications for our lives to the Jews and the Greeks.

282
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:53,600
The first thing that's offensive about that is he's preaching the same message of salvation to both of these groups of people.

283
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,660
And the Jews are like, no, no, no, no, no.

284
00:19:55,660 --> 00:19:56,900
We're God's people.

285
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:57,840
We're special.

286
00:19:57,840 --> 00:19:59,420
This message is for us first.

287
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:00,700
Maybe they can have it later.

288
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:01,760
But right now it's for us.

289
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:03,820
And Saul says, no, it's for both of you.

290
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:06,540
And this is the message.

291
00:20:06,540 --> 00:20:07,500
First, repentance.

292
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:14,380
All of us who have grown up in church know that repentance means to change your mind, right?

293
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:16,320
To change your mind.

294
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:17,760
But he adds a clarifier here.

295
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,380
Towards God.

296
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:22,620
Change your mind and go in the right direction.

297
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:24,600
Repentance towards God.

298
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:31,180
And then faith, which Michelle did a really good job of covering last week, is way more than just intellectual belief.

299
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:33,160
Remember she said that the demons believe?

300
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:37,500
Faith is so much more than just intellectual belief.

301
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:39,820
It is a strong conviction.

302
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:43,140
Sometimes it carries the weight of fidelity or loyalty.

303
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:49,300
Caesar would actually proclaim to his people, Caesar is Lord.

304
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:52,720
Place your faith, your pistis in me as Lord.

305
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:55,480
It was a political statement of authority.

306
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:59,800
And Paul is saying, no, no one but Jesus is Lord.

307
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:03,520
You place your allegiance, your faith, your trust in him.

308
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:09,260
Now, with that little bit unpacked, can we begin to see how it might have been offensive to some?

309
00:21:09,260 --> 00:21:12,500
It's not just a generic spiritual phrase.

310
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:17,460
It is a declaration of where the direction of your life is headed.

311
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:19,320
Of who are you submitting to?

312
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:21,800
Where is your authority being placed?

313
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:31,040
Saul says, if you want to follow Jesus, you place your allegiance in him as Lord, master, owner, the one who gets to call the shots.

314
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:36,100
This is not a neutered spiritual word that we sing, but a powerful and practical and even political world.

315
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:40,820
Every other authority figure takes the back seat to Jesus if you want to follow him.

316
00:21:41,620 --> 00:21:46,660
So, this message can become a little bit offensive to some.

317
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:54,000
I want to unpack how in which the Jews and the Gentiles were offended in different ways.

318
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:57,140
Because they were offended in different ways.

319
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:58,240
First, the Jews.

320
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:05,160
The Jews had a religious nature, a prideful nature.

321
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:07,980
So, the first reason the Jews were offended was because of their pride.

322
00:22:07,980 --> 00:22:11,520
They had been set apart as God's people for thousands of years.

323
00:22:11,520 --> 00:22:18,280
And they forgot that their whole reason God set them apart was so that they could be a blessing to the rest of the world.

324
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:18,880
Right?

325
00:22:18,940 --> 00:22:20,040
This is what God tells Abraham.

326
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:21,120
I'm going to bless you.

327
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:22,660
I'm going to create a nation through you.

328
00:22:22,660 --> 00:22:25,040
And through that nation, you will bless the rest of the world.

329
00:22:25,040 --> 00:22:28,660
But they'd lost sight of that promise.

330
00:22:28,660 --> 00:22:33,100
And they were prideful about their way of salvation.

331
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:37,260
And when Paul came and proclaimed the same message of salvation to the Jews and to the Greeks,

332
00:22:37,260 --> 00:22:38,960
all you have to do is repent.

333
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:42,700
Change your mind towards God and place your faith and trust in Jesus.

334
00:22:42,700 --> 00:22:43,860
The Jews were like, no.

335
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:46,980
They have to get circumcised and they have to obey the Mosaic law.

336
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:52,960
Paul's like, no, if that happened, if that's how they would receive the message of salvation,

337
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:54,160
then nothing has changed.

338
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:59,120
Because there was a way in which Gentiles could receive salvation in the Old Testament.

339
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:03,480
It was by getting circumcised and obeying all the Mosaic laws.

340
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,700
And the Jews are like, yeah, exactly.

341
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:08,680
If they want to be a part of us, they have to do all the things that we're doing.

342
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:11,240
And this is what Paul would say to that.

343
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:14,260
He says, in his writing to the Galatians, he says,

344
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:18,620
if righteousness comes through the law, then Christ died for no purpose.

345
00:23:18,620 --> 00:23:20,900
So he's telling the Jews, no.

346
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:26,080
If they're just receiving the message of salvation through circumcision and obedience to the law,

347
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:27,860
then why did God even send Jesus?

348
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:29,680
What's the whole point of this whole thing?

349
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:33,380
So the Jews are offended with pride.

350
00:23:33,380 --> 00:23:40,540
And I think more importantly, and I think this is the one that has more of an application to the American church,

351
00:23:40,540 --> 00:23:44,740
is the Jews were very afraid at this time.

352
00:23:45,740 --> 00:23:48,400
This was a very volatile time in the Roman Empire.

353
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:53,480
And the Jews had a really, they had a unique exemption with the Roman government

354
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:57,080
that allowed them not to worship any of the other Roman gods.

355
00:23:57,080 --> 00:24:03,400
They were the religion, the nation that was allowed to just worship their God.

356
00:24:04,140 --> 00:24:09,060
And now this new group of people, these new Christians, they are saying,

357
00:24:09,060 --> 00:24:11,280
wait a second, we also only have one God.

358
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:13,060
We are not going to worship the Roman gods.

359
00:24:13,060 --> 00:24:16,280
And now the Romans have a problem and the Jews have a problem.

360
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:17,340
Okay?

361
00:24:17,340 --> 00:24:20,400
Because there was so much going on in this culture.

362
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:27,040
And the Romans were already kind of regretting their decision to let the Jews not worship the Roman gods.

363
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:32,740
And now there's a new group that's saying, we're not with them, but we also don't want to worship your gods.

364
00:24:32,740 --> 00:24:36,440
Now there was some really loaded political ramifications there.

365
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:42,820
And so the Jews were reacting out of fear because they were like, look, if this group continues to grow,

366
00:24:42,820 --> 00:24:45,540
then the Romans are going to cut us all off.

367
00:24:45,540 --> 00:24:47,600
They're going to persecute us.

368
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:49,080
They're not going to let us worship God.

369
00:24:49,080 --> 00:24:50,520
They're not going to let us come to the temple.

370
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:53,280
They're not going to let us do our sacrificial systems.

371
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:55,280
And guess what happened?

372
00:24:55,740 --> 00:24:58,860
All of that, all of these fears happened around 70 AD, right?

373
00:24:58,860 --> 00:25:00,260
Like this stuff happened.

374
00:25:00,260 --> 00:25:05,780
The Jews had a good idea of what was going to happen if these Christians kept growing,

375
00:25:05,780 --> 00:25:10,160
kept becoming more and more important.

376
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:20,380
And I think, I think this temptation, this fear, this reason that we can tend to drift away from obedience to the gospel

377
00:25:20,380 --> 00:25:23,900
is still true of Christians in America today.

378
00:25:23,900 --> 00:25:31,240
See, Christians in America, we've had a unique position of influence and power in our culture throughout the history of our nation.

379
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:32,080
Can we agree with that?

380
00:25:32,080 --> 00:25:39,720
And as the culture rejects Christian ideas more and more, I see so many Christians, listen to this, this is so important.

381
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:45,660
I see so many Christians responding out of, responding in anger fueled by fear.

382
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:51,200
We get angry, we yell, we yell, we scream, we throw stones.

383
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:52,100
Why do we do it?

384
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:53,960
We do it because we're afraid.

385
00:25:53,960 --> 00:26:01,300
We're afraid as the nation becomes less and less Christian, as the nation becomes more and more anti-Christian,

386
00:26:01,300 --> 00:26:05,060
we're worried that our comfort is going to go away.

387
00:26:05,060 --> 00:26:07,420
Our influence is going to go away.

388
00:26:07,420 --> 00:26:09,360
Our power is going to go away.

389
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:12,340
And we've become more worried about our comfort than our testimony.

390
00:26:12,340 --> 00:26:19,000
We need to remember this, church, that Jesus will build his church.

391
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:21,780
And the gates of hell will not prevail against it.

392
00:26:21,780 --> 00:26:23,920
But listen to me, listen to me, listen to me.

393
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:29,340
He does not need us to be influential in our culture in order for him to build his church.

394
00:26:33,460 --> 00:26:38,360
That's like upside down from all of our businesses and political ideologies.

395
00:26:38,360 --> 00:26:42,840
Like in America, what do you need in order to be, to make a difference?

396
00:26:42,840 --> 00:26:43,920
You need influence.

397
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:44,860
You need power.

398
00:26:44,860 --> 00:26:48,360
The kingdom of God is upside down from that.

399
00:26:48,360 --> 00:26:53,960
Jesus does not need us to be influential or powerful in order to make a difference in our community.

400
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:58,900
Here's the reality is that the church actually grows way more throughout history

401
00:26:58,900 --> 00:27:01,400
when they're being persecuted and pushed to the margins.

402
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:03,120
Do you know why?

403
00:27:04,380 --> 00:27:08,840
Because when the church is persecuted and pushed to the margins, guess who doesn't come to church anymore?

404
00:27:08,840 --> 00:27:17,680
The Christians that don't actually believe that Jesus is Lord and gets to call the shots in their life.

405
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:28,540
And so, I think, like the Jews, the American church has become fearful of losing our influence.

406
00:27:29,320 --> 00:27:37,300
We try and grasp at it through our democracy, through who we vote for, through our social media influence.

407
00:27:37,300 --> 00:27:42,920
And I'm just like, I'm stepping back and looking at even Christian leaders on social media.

408
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:47,260
And we're just so fearful that we're going to lose power and control.

409
00:27:47,260 --> 00:27:53,880
And I'm just not sold that us losing power and control isn't actually good for the health of the church

410
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:57,820
and our influence and our country moving forward.

411
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,820
Jesus doesn't need us to be influential.

412
00:28:00,820 --> 00:28:02,220
He needs us to be obedient.

413
00:28:02,220 --> 00:28:06,320
And the church actually tends to flourish way more when it's persecuted

414
00:28:06,320 --> 00:28:09,260
and pushed outside the positions of culture and political influence.

415
00:28:09,260 --> 00:28:15,060
Are we willing to repent, to change our ideas about how God can work in our culture?

416
00:28:15,920 --> 00:28:22,980
Are we willing to submit to Jesus as Lord and realize that he might be having the most impact

417
00:28:22,980 --> 00:28:29,580
through us laying down our privileges and our power in order to serve those on the margins?

418
00:28:29,580 --> 00:28:30,860
All right.

419
00:28:30,860 --> 00:28:35,560
So, that's how the Jews were offended by Paul's message to repent, to turn towards God,

420
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:40,160
to place your faith and trust in Jesus alone as Lord and master of your life.

421
00:28:40,520 --> 00:28:42,280
And this is why the Gentiles got offended.

422
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:45,840
Do I have time for that?

423
00:28:45,840 --> 00:28:48,100
No, let's skip that one.

424
00:28:48,100 --> 00:28:48,340
All right.

425
00:28:48,340 --> 00:28:49,500
Idolatry, right?

426
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:52,460
So, the Gentiles, they loved the gods.

427
00:28:52,460 --> 00:28:58,820
They were usually really open-minded to adding more and more gods to their menu of gods.

428
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:05,260
And so, here's the thing that made Paul's message, the gospel of Jesus, so offensive to the Gentiles

429
00:29:05,260 --> 00:29:10,420
because Paul did not say Jesus is a Son of God that demands your worship.

430
00:29:11,060 --> 00:29:14,600
If Paul would have said Jesus is a Son of God that demands your worship,

431
00:29:14,600 --> 00:29:16,360
the Gentiles would have been like, sounds great.

432
00:29:16,360 --> 00:29:17,380
Where do we put his statue?

433
00:29:17,380 --> 00:29:20,420
What kind of sacrifice does he want?

434
00:29:20,420 --> 00:29:22,040
What kind of incense does he want us to burn?

435
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:22,860
Give us the rules.

436
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:24,220
Tell us the things and we'll do it.

437
00:29:24,220 --> 00:29:25,460
But that's not the message.

438
00:29:25,460 --> 00:29:32,220
The message is Jesus alone is the Lord, the master, the Son of God.

439
00:29:32,220 --> 00:29:36,240
And if you want to follow him, you have to get rid of all of your other gods.

440
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:40,560
You have to place your faith, your trust, your allegiance in him alone.

441
00:29:40,560 --> 00:29:42,160
Not only do you have to get rid of all other gods,

442
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:45,820
you've got to get rid of Rome as the supreme authority and leader of your life.

443
00:29:45,820 --> 00:29:50,840
Jesus has to be the supreme authority of your life.

444
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:54,460
And does that now make sense why some Gentiles would be offended by that?

445
00:29:54,460 --> 00:29:57,660
Idolatry.

446
00:29:57,660 --> 00:29:59,780
The Gentiles loved the gods.

447
00:29:59,780 --> 00:30:07,700
And they would have added Jesus willingly as long as he didn't demand supreme loyalty.

448
00:30:08,300 --> 00:30:10,820
Now, do we see where I'm going with this?

449
00:30:10,820 --> 00:30:16,640
Many secular people in our nation today still respond this way to Jesus.

450
00:30:16,640 --> 00:30:22,520
They're fine with Jesus plus whatever other things they've got going on in their life.

451
00:30:22,520 --> 00:30:29,820
Many of us in the church today are fine with Jesus plus whatever other things that we have going on in our life,

452
00:30:29,820 --> 00:30:32,920
whatever ideologies, political beliefs, whatever it is.

453
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:36,980
So many of us are great with Jesus plus.

454
00:30:37,100 --> 00:30:40,940
The problem with that is Paul's message is not Jesus plus, it's Jesus alone.

455
00:30:40,940 --> 00:30:51,820
A lot of Americans are willing to embrace Jesus as a significant part of their lives,

456
00:30:51,820 --> 00:30:57,800
but it's offensive and oppressive to suggest that Jesus is the way, the truth, and the life.

457
00:30:57,800 --> 00:31:05,040
Many of us are willing to add Jesus to our worldview as long as it means Jesus plus.

458
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:10,880
I'll give some examples just so that you know where I'm headed and we can be all offended equally.

459
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:15,600
Jesus plus nationalism.

460
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:19,420
Jesus plus progressivism.

461
00:31:19,420 --> 00:31:23,580
Jesus plus individualism.

462
00:31:24,860 --> 00:31:30,080
As long as I get to hold on to the thing that I like most about being American,

463
00:31:30,080 --> 00:31:33,180
the thing that I like most that makes me most comfortable,

464
00:31:33,180 --> 00:31:36,440
as long as Jesus doesn't tell me that some of those things aren't true.

465
00:31:36,440 --> 00:31:42,700
And here's the thing where it gets slippery is all of those ideologies have glimpses of truth,

466
00:31:42,700 --> 00:31:46,100
and so we embrace the part of Jesus that affirms those things,

467
00:31:46,100 --> 00:31:50,640
and we ignore the part of Jesus that calls us for our own idolatry and rebellion.

468
00:31:52,680 --> 00:31:59,540
And if we want to actually follow Jesus, we've got to allow him to call us on the false beliefs and ideologies that we're holding on to.

469
00:31:59,540 --> 00:32:04,300
We love the Jesus that believes everything that we believe.

470
00:32:07,620 --> 00:32:10,520
I love the Jesus that believes everything that I believe,

471
00:32:10,520 --> 00:32:13,880
which is why a diverse community of believers is so important,

472
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:18,220
because I need people who think differently than me and love me and love Jesus to say,

473
00:32:18,220 --> 00:32:20,120
dude, you've got some blind spots over here.

474
00:32:21,100 --> 00:32:25,040
We all need each other because all of us have blind spots.

475
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:34,360
And we're really good at just listening to the voice of Jesus that agrees with everything that we're already doing and thinking and believing.

476
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:46,260
Paul's gospel is offensive to the proud and fearful religious as well as a sophisticated and open-minded secularist,

477
00:32:46,260 --> 00:32:47,360
but it is life.

478
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:51,900
It is life to those of us who are willing to receive it with humility,

479
00:32:51,900 --> 00:32:55,520
to lay down our old ideologies and lifestyles,

480
00:32:55,520 --> 00:32:58,840
and to embrace Jesus as the supreme Lord and leader of our life.

481
00:32:58,900 --> 00:33:00,620
I love how Paul puts it in 1 Corinthians.

482
00:33:00,620 --> 00:33:03,360
For the Jews demand signs,

483
00:33:03,360 --> 00:33:05,820
the Greeks seek wisdom,

484
00:33:05,820 --> 00:33:08,480
but we preach Christ crucified,

485
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:12,520
a stumbling block to the Jews and folly to the Gentiles,

486
00:33:12,520 --> 00:33:14,040
but to those of us who are called,

487
00:33:14,040 --> 00:33:15,400
both Jews and Greeks,

488
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:19,200
Christ is the power and the wisdom of God.

489
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:21,860
Paul's saying it's foolish,

490
00:33:21,860 --> 00:33:26,800
it's offensive to religious Jews who are fearful and trying to hold on to power.

491
00:33:27,420 --> 00:33:30,740
It's offensive to secular Gentiles who are just,

492
00:33:30,740 --> 00:33:31,880
they want wisdom,

493
00:33:31,880 --> 00:33:33,140
they want it to all make sense,

494
00:33:33,140 --> 00:33:34,520
they want it to all add up.

495
00:33:34,520 --> 00:33:38,440
Paul says it doesn't all add up.

496
00:33:38,440 --> 00:33:42,360
The gospel demands the response of us laying down our life.

497
00:33:42,360 --> 00:33:44,760
It doesn't make sense to the culture,

498
00:33:44,760 --> 00:33:48,040
but it is truth and will lead to life.

499
00:33:48,040 --> 00:33:51,500
Paul then,

500
00:33:51,500 --> 00:33:53,160
that's his message,

501
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:53,960
why it's offensive.

502
00:33:57,420 --> 00:33:57,740
Oh,

503
00:33:57,740 --> 00:33:58,900
I'm going way too far,

504
00:33:58,900 --> 00:33:59,560
way too fast.

505
00:33:59,560 --> 00:34:00,040
Sorry.

506
00:34:00,040 --> 00:34:04,480
He then goes on to,

507
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:07,600
to just double down on why all of this matters.

508
00:34:07,600 --> 00:34:09,420
He shares his value system,

509
00:34:09,420 --> 00:34:10,500
his value structure.

510
00:34:10,500 --> 00:34:12,040
Verse 24,

511
00:34:12,040 --> 00:34:15,120
I do not count my life of any value,

512
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:16,980
nor as precious to myself,

513
00:34:16,980 --> 00:34:21,000
if only I may finish my course in the ministry that I have received from the Lord Jesus,

514
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:25,080
to testify to the gospel of the grace of our God.

515
00:34:25,080 --> 00:34:26,340
Saying,

516
00:34:26,340 --> 00:34:26,560
look,

517
00:34:26,560 --> 00:34:28,120
I'm cool with being persecuted.

518
00:34:28,120 --> 00:34:29,900
I'm cool with being thrown out of cities.

519
00:34:29,900 --> 00:34:31,820
I'm cool with being stoned and left for dead,

520
00:34:31,820 --> 00:34:33,340
because this life,

521
00:34:33,340 --> 00:34:36,700
this temporary earthly life is not all that matters.

522
00:34:36,700 --> 00:34:40,060
There is an eternity that is coming that my hope is in,

523
00:34:40,060 --> 00:34:42,220
and I am okay with suffering and being persecuted.

524
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:45,620
I'm okay with being laughed at,

525
00:34:45,620 --> 00:34:46,120
rejected,

526
00:34:46,120 --> 00:34:46,900
and mocked,

527
00:34:46,900 --> 00:34:50,020
because my life is not invested in just here and now.

528
00:34:50,020 --> 00:34:51,660
My life is invested in eternity.

529
00:34:51,660 --> 00:34:54,020
This is Paul's value system.

530
00:34:54,020 --> 00:34:56,020
This is what drives Paul's decision-making.

531
00:34:56,020 --> 00:34:58,460
The gospel that,

532
00:34:58,460 --> 00:35:00,840
that the gospel of Jesus that Paul preaches,

533
00:35:00,840 --> 00:35:05,700
emphasizes the importance of eternal value over any earthly or temporary gain.

534
00:35:05,700 --> 00:35:08,160
Because of the hope of the resurrection.

535
00:35:08,160 --> 00:35:09,260
Look,

536
00:35:09,260 --> 00:35:11,580
we see this in Paul's own response to the gospel.

537
00:35:12,180 --> 00:35:14,080
Before Paul submitted his life to Jesus,

538
00:35:14,080 --> 00:35:15,980
he was a man of power and influence.

539
00:35:15,980 --> 00:35:21,040
He was a religious leader that got all kinds of praise from all kinds of people.

540
00:35:21,040 --> 00:35:21,880
And he said,

541
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:22,400
you know what?

542
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:24,260
All of that was worthless.

543
00:35:24,260 --> 00:35:25,740
Later,

544
00:35:25,740 --> 00:35:26,720
he'll call it rubbish,

545
00:35:26,720 --> 00:35:27,540
garbage.

546
00:35:27,540 --> 00:35:33,600
None of it matters in light of the eternal hope of the resurrection of Jesus.

547
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:36,000
The reason that Paul is okay with being,

548
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:41,800
with offending people and being rejected with tears and with pain is because all of it is

549
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:44,620
an investment in the eternal hope of Jesus.

550
00:35:44,620 --> 00:35:46,840
All right.

551
00:35:46,840 --> 00:35:50,020
So that's Paul's summary of how he did ministry,

552
00:35:50,020 --> 00:35:51,600
why he did ministry,

553
00:35:51,600 --> 00:35:52,160
what he said,

554
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:54,960
how it offended all of the people that he interacted with.

555
00:35:54,960 --> 00:35:55,500
Now,

556
00:35:55,500 --> 00:35:58,020
he's going to look the leaders of the Ephesian church in the eye,

557
00:35:58,020 --> 00:35:59,080
and he's going to give them a warning.

558
00:35:59,080 --> 00:35:59,920
He says,

559
00:35:59,920 --> 00:36:00,120
look,

560
00:36:00,120 --> 00:36:01,360
I've done everything I could do.

561
00:36:01,660 --> 00:36:03,060
I have to leave now.

562
00:36:03,060 --> 00:36:05,560
And you guys are in charge.

563
00:36:05,560 --> 00:36:10,460
So this is his final warning to the leaders of the Ephesian church.

564
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:11,160
Verse 25.

565
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:13,940
He says,

566
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:14,560
And now behold,

567
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:20,440
I know that none of you among whom I have gone about proclaiming the kingdom of God will ever see my face again.

568
00:36:20,440 --> 00:36:20,740
Therefore,

569
00:36:20,740 --> 00:36:23,680
I testify to you this day that I am innocent of the blood.

570
00:36:23,680 --> 00:36:25,040
I've told you everything that I can tell you,

571
00:36:25,040 --> 00:36:27,460
how you respond to it is of utmost importance.

572
00:36:27,460 --> 00:36:31,260
I did not shrink back from declaring to you the whole counsel of God.

573
00:36:31,380 --> 00:36:31,580
Therefore,

574
00:36:31,580 --> 00:36:35,160
pay careful attention to yourselves and to all the flock,

575
00:36:35,160 --> 00:36:37,700
which the Holy Spirit has made you overseers,

576
00:36:37,700 --> 00:36:38,940
to care for the church of God,

577
00:36:38,940 --> 00:36:41,380
which is obtained by his own blood.

578
00:36:41,380 --> 00:36:43,740
I know that after my departure,

579
00:36:43,740 --> 00:36:45,500
fierce wolves will come in among you,

580
00:36:45,500 --> 00:36:46,560
not sparing the flock.

581
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:52,400
And from among your own selves will arise men speaking twisted things to draw away the disciples after them.

582
00:36:52,400 --> 00:36:52,760
Therefore,

583
00:36:52,760 --> 00:36:53,360
be alert.

584
00:36:53,360 --> 00:36:55,420
All right.

585
00:36:55,420 --> 00:36:55,940
So,

586
00:36:55,940 --> 00:36:57,320
I am.

587
00:36:57,320 --> 00:36:59,220
We've got to go fast.

588
00:37:00,140 --> 00:37:01,460
You guys put your seatbelts on for me?

589
00:37:01,460 --> 00:37:03,560
All right.

590
00:37:03,560 --> 00:37:03,760
So,

591
00:37:03,760 --> 00:37:04,540
he gives some,

592
00:37:04,540 --> 00:37:07,620
he gives some exhortations and some warnings.

593
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:09,380
First,

594
00:37:09,380 --> 00:37:10,100
his exhortations.

595
00:37:10,100 --> 00:37:16,420
He tells the leaders that he has taught them everything they need to know and what they need to do with that information is ultimately on them.

596
00:37:16,420 --> 00:37:19,360
And the first,

597
00:37:19,360 --> 00:37:21,860
the top priority that he gives to them is he says,

598
00:37:21,860 --> 00:37:25,300
pay attention to yourselves,

599
00:37:25,300 --> 00:37:27,900
to your own lives.

600
00:37:27,900 --> 00:37:29,740
The top priority for Paul,

601
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:32,920
if the church is going to be healthy and successful moving forward,

602
00:37:32,920 --> 00:37:35,500
if the Ephesian church is going to last persecution,

603
00:37:35,500 --> 00:37:36,820
last difficulty,

604
00:37:36,820 --> 00:37:37,920
last challenges,

605
00:37:37,920 --> 00:37:43,820
the first thing that has to happen is the leaders of the church have to prioritize personal faithfulness.

606
00:37:43,820 --> 00:37:45,800
They have to be holy.

607
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:48,360
They have to be obedient to the teachings of Scripture.

608
00:37:52,360 --> 00:37:57,040
Does this sound like it might be a priority that the American church might need to embrace?

609
00:37:57,040 --> 00:38:00,900
See,

610
00:38:00,900 --> 00:38:04,500
it's very easy for church leaders to get so focused on the tasks of ministry.

611
00:38:04,500 --> 00:38:08,380
And this is the part of the sermon that I'm going to preach to myself and the few leaders in the room.

612
00:38:09,500 --> 00:38:11,800
I think it has implications for the rest of us,

613
00:38:11,800 --> 00:38:15,400
but I'm just going to call myself out for a minute and then we'll get back to you.

614
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:15,840
All right.

615
00:38:17,040 --> 00:38:24,060
It's very easy for church leaders to get so focused on the tasks of ministry that we neglect our relationship with and obedience to God.

616
00:38:25,160 --> 00:38:32,480
We use the fruit of our ministry to justify our lack of character and it's killing the church.

617
00:38:32,480 --> 00:38:35,460
Just this week,

618
00:38:35,460 --> 00:38:37,380
as I was preparing the sermon this week,

619
00:38:37,380 --> 00:38:40,440
another very well-known church leader.

620
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:45,120
It came out that he had hidden sin in his life from years and years ago.

621
00:38:45,120 --> 00:38:46,040
It finally came out.

622
00:38:46,040 --> 00:38:53,760
People are leaving the church in droves because of the hypocrisy of Christian leaders.

623
00:38:55,160 --> 00:38:57,780
And Paul says,

624
00:38:57,780 --> 00:39:00,340
if you want to be successful,

625
00:39:00,340 --> 00:39:02,900
if you want the fruit of your ministry to last,

626
00:39:02,900 --> 00:39:03,340
leaders,

627
00:39:03,340 --> 00:39:05,520
you've got to pay attention to your life,

628
00:39:05,520 --> 00:39:07,100
to your obedience,

629
00:39:07,100 --> 00:39:08,800
to your faithfulness,

630
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:09,480
to your holiness.

631
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:14,620
You can't get so consumed with ministry that you forget about your relationship with God.

632
00:39:14,620 --> 00:39:19,800
We shouldn't expect perfection from our leaders,

633
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:21,200
but we should expect honesty,

634
00:39:21,200 --> 00:39:21,800
confession,

635
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:22,480
and accountability.

636
00:39:23,740 --> 00:39:29,920
But because we've allowed our leaders to elevate their title to an identity and their paycheck as necessity,

637
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:32,940
it often encourages cover-ups and justifications.

638
00:39:32,940 --> 00:39:38,260
This is like a message to a pastor's conference,

639
00:39:38,260 --> 00:39:39,460
so I'll move on quickly.

640
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:39,840
All right.

641
00:39:39,840 --> 00:39:41,080
But this happens.

642
00:39:41,080 --> 00:39:43,860
Carl Vader says this.

643
00:39:43,860 --> 00:39:44,200
He says,

644
00:39:44,200 --> 00:39:46,520
integrity is the new competency.

645
00:39:48,820 --> 00:39:50,240
Integrity is the new competency.

646
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:56,180
If the church wants people from the outside to look at us and to give us a voice in our life,

647
00:39:56,180 --> 00:39:59,540
the most important thing is that we have integrity.

648
00:39:59,540 --> 00:40:01,040
See,

649
00:40:01,040 --> 00:40:02,340
the generation before us,

650
00:40:02,340 --> 00:40:05,080
before me,

651
00:40:05,080 --> 00:40:07,000
I don't know why I did that to all of you.

652
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:08,040
The generation before me,

653
00:40:08,040 --> 00:40:10,260
competency was so important,

654
00:40:10,260 --> 00:40:10,480
right?

655
00:40:10,540 --> 00:40:11,800
Like businesses were growing,

656
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:12,520
expanding,

657
00:40:12,520 --> 00:40:13,420
booming.

658
00:40:13,420 --> 00:40:16,560
What we needed from our leaders is that they knew how to lead.

659
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:19,120
But guess where that led us?

660
00:40:19,120 --> 00:40:22,240
We had a lot of really good leaders with no character,

661
00:40:22,240 --> 00:40:23,380
no morality.

662
00:40:23,380 --> 00:40:26,200
And now my generation is looking at that and saying,

663
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:26,380
look,

664
00:40:26,380 --> 00:40:28,020
we don't care if you're a good leader or not.

665
00:40:28,020 --> 00:40:28,760
Are you genuine?

666
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:29,740
Are you authentic?

667
00:40:29,740 --> 00:40:30,700
Are you honest?

668
00:40:32,900 --> 00:40:34,940
So this is what we need from our church leaders.

669
00:40:34,940 --> 00:40:35,700
We need integrity.

670
00:40:35,700 --> 00:40:37,060
He tells Paul,

671
00:40:37,060 --> 00:40:39,380
not only do you have to look out for your life,

672
00:40:39,380 --> 00:40:41,720
but you have to look out for the life of the rest of the flock.

673
00:40:41,720 --> 00:40:48,860
Pay careful attention to yourselves and to all the flock in which the Holy Spirit made you overseers.

674
00:40:48,860 --> 00:40:52,860
Not only is faithful obedience a top priority of church leaders,

675
00:40:52,860 --> 00:40:57,440
but it's a top priority for all of you sitting in this room that would consider yourself a follower of Jesus.

676
00:40:57,440 --> 00:41:01,380
We need to become,

677
00:41:01,380 --> 00:41:01,880
listen to this.

678
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:02,240
This is,

679
00:41:02,240 --> 00:41:03,940
I'm going to go on a rant real quick.

680
00:41:03,940 --> 00:41:10,600
We need to become less obsessed with getting our theology perfect and more obsessed with getting our obedience on track.

681
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:16,800
Notice the first thing that Paul says to the church and to the leaders is not make sure your doctrine is perfect.

682
00:41:16,800 --> 00:41:22,480
The first thing that he says is make sure that you keep track of your obedience.

683
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:26,700
And we get this flip-flop in the American church.

684
00:41:26,700 --> 00:41:27,760
Guess what he's going to say next?

685
00:41:27,760 --> 00:41:28,520
Spoiler alert.

686
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:30,720
He's going to say doctrine is important,

687
00:41:30,860 --> 00:41:32,540
but it's secondary to obedience.

688
00:41:32,540 --> 00:41:39,860
We need to become less obsessed with getting our theology perfect and more obsessed with getting our obedience on track.

689
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:45,160
Because the church of Jesus is the most valuable asset of the kingdom of God on earth.

690
00:41:45,160 --> 00:41:50,980
He says it's been bought with the precious blood of Jesus.

691
00:41:52,640 --> 00:41:55,980
And what Jesus wants for his church is obedience.

692
00:41:55,980 --> 00:41:57,560
And what Jesus wants for his church is obedience, is submission, is faith.

693
00:41:57,560 --> 00:42:04,660
Nothing will render us less effective than if we neglect faithful obedience to the teachings and examples of Jesus.

694
00:42:06,180 --> 00:42:08,820
You guys have heard me talk about golf on stage.

695
00:42:08,820 --> 00:42:11,860
I won't bore you to death.

696
00:42:11,860 --> 00:42:15,240
But any of you that golf know that golf is a very hard sport.

697
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:23,460
And almost nobody that I golf with, almost nobody in this room who golf knows anything about golf.

698
00:42:23,460 --> 00:42:25,460
It's so hard.

699
00:42:25,460 --> 00:42:26,580
It's so technical.

700
00:42:27,300 --> 00:42:36,880
And you know what is infuriating as a golfer is to stand up on the tee, make a bad shot, and then have the person behind you tell you what you did wrong.

701
00:42:37,980 --> 00:42:42,940
When you and they both know that you all stink at golf.

702
00:42:42,940 --> 00:42:48,320
So it's like, you're going to tell me how to golf, right?

